    "collapsible_content_EXiNNx": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_TxEjiH": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does MeowGo G40 Pro support physical cards?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, MeowGo G40 Pro supports physical SlM card. You can insert a physical SIM card into the device to get internet access. Except using the physical SlM card, you can also buy our data plan from specific country to global coverage. To view our different travel data plans for different countries, please visit our <a href=\"https://store.glocalme.com/collections/data-package\" title=\"https://store.glocalme.com/collections/data-package\">Data Plans</a> page.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_8ncNTM": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is there a user manual for the MeowGo G40 Pro?",
            "answer": "<p>We are sorry that the user manual for the MeowGo G40 Pro is not available now. Actually the user manual is the same as the G4 Pro. You can also check it from <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0658/8963/2410/files/G4P.pdf?v=1745475415\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0658/8963/2410/files/G4P.pdf?v=1745475415\">here</a>.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_VTYTzb": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Numen Air and the new MeowGo G40 Pro?",
            "answer": "<p>MeowGo G40 Pro is a 4G device, Numen Air is a 5G device. Numen Air is the best seller on our website, not only supports 5G but also 4G/3G, if you go to a place without a 5G signal, you can also use the 4G data plan, and the speed will be faster than using the 4G data plan in a 4G device.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_BcYxCK": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How many devices can I connect at once, and will the speed drop a lot?",
            "answer": "<p>MeowGo G40 Pro can connect up to 10 devices. It’s Wi‑Fi 5 with 4G CAT‑13 (up to 390 Mbps down/150 Mbps up), so for typical use (email, video calls, streaming) it should be smooth for a small group. If all 10 are streaming HD at once, I should expect some slowdown.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_DqNXUL": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the battery really last for my day out?",
            "answer": "<p>The built‑in 3200 mAh battery is rated up to around 13–15 hours. For a full workday with a laptop and phone connected, I can reasonably expect it to last through meetings and commuting; heavy video streaming or tethering many devices will shorten that time. It charges via Type-C (10W input).</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_DWdHKz": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does “4G Qualcomm Snapdragon” mean for my everyday use?",
            "answer": "<p>It’s powered by the Qualcomm QCM2290 platform, so you can get a stable 4G CAT‑13 connection with efficient power usage. In daily use, that translates to quicker network attach, more consistent speeds for video calls/streams, and better battery efficiency compared with older chipsets.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_KH3PfY": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it work when I travel internationally?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. It covers 200+ countries and regions and can switch among multiple mobile operators automatically with HyperConn. I can check specific availability with the Country Checker and use the included Global 1GB (90‑day) gift to get started.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        },
        "accordion_ytfftY": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How seamless is the connection in daily use (subway, office, café)?",
            "answer": "<p>The HyperConn technology constantly evaluates networks and can switch between 4G/3G/Wi‑Fi for the best link, aiming to keep me online without manual fiddling. In practice, I may notice brief handoff delays in weak‑signal areas (elevators, underground), but it’s designed to minimize drops and keep a reliable connection for work and streaming.</p>",
            "opened": false
          }
        }
      },
